slide('Incident-to eligibility requires an established treatment relationship','Medicare office rules require more than an available physician.',cards(('Treatment involvement','The physician initiated the course of treatment and remains actively involved.'),('Qualifying service','The follow-up fits the established plan and satisfies the other incident-to requirements.'),('Supervision','Required direct supervision and the billing/employment arrangement must be satisfied.'))+reveal('2026 supervision detail','For applicable incident-to services, immediate availability can use real-time audio/video, not audio-only. The 2026 rule excludes services with 010- or 090-day global surgery indicators from this virtual-supervision policy. This does not remove other eligibility requirements.')+call('A new problem or treatment change requires reassessment; do not rely only on “established patient” status.'),['R5','R14','R6'],'04 / Physician–APP collaboration')
slide('A co-signature does not establish physician billing','The record must show the work and a qualifying billing pathway.',cards(('APP contribution','Identify the evaluation, decisions and eligible time actually furnished.'),('Physician contribution','Document any personal work or qualifying supervisory role.'),('Claim pathway','Choose direct billing or another pathway only when its requirements are met.'))+call('“Reviewed and agree” is not a substitute for incident-to eligibility or personally performed substantive work.'),['R5','R11'],'04 / Physician–APP collaboration')
slide('Split/shared E/M belongs to eligible facility encounters','Medicare office visits are not split/shared visits.',cards(('Eligible setting + team','Physician and APP in the same group; a qualifying facility E/M service.'),('Substantive portion','For noncritical E/M: more than half of combined distinct time OR substantive MDM under the applicable definition.'),('Claim + record','Identify both clinicians; billing clinician signs/dates. Use that NPI and modifier FS.'))+call('Count overlapping time once. Critical care uses the time rule. A hospital-owned clinic is not automatically a facility setting; verify actual place of service.'),['R11','R2'],'04 / Physician–APP collaboration')
